R33 Rust patch proposal — BLOCKED at the snapshot-token owner

No applicable source diff is emitted from the pinned archive. The archive has
no source-grounded, serializable HIR snapshot token and does not include the
`super::program::RuntimeProgram` definition/construction owner. Inserting a
guessed accessor or a made-up token into `machine.rs` would fabricate the
missing premise. The exact prerequisite and bounded decoder proposal follow.

Required owner addition before this proposal can become an applicable diff:

1. At the constructor that binds the immutable HIR to
   `super::program::RuntimeProgram`, mint one opaque `HirSnapshotToken` for
   that HIR snapshot and retain it on that owner. Its creation/equality must
   distinguish separate HIR owners even when their declaration indices and
   source text match. It must not be reconstructed from Debug output,
   `SourceNodeKey` Debug, module spelling, a declaration index, or source
   spans. The constructor is not present in either pinned archive member, so
   its API and available source identity cannot be safely specified here.
2. Have `Machine::callback_route_json` obtain that token from its held
   `Arc<RuntimeProgram>` and put the same token beside every effect-family and
   operation coordinate, including the full permission-family row. The
   request, consumer, selected resolved operation, and row must all be emitted
   from the same immutable owner. Keep the selected arm's `SourceNodeKey`
   Debug field explicitly presentation-only; it is not made into an operation
   or snapshot identity.
3. Decode against the `RuntimeProgram`/HIR owner carrying the expected token:

   ```text
   decode_family(owner, (token, family_index)):
       require token == owner.hir_snapshot_token else ForeignSnapshot
       return owner.hir.source_effect_declarations().get(family_index)
           .map(clone typed SourceEffectId) or FamilyOutOfRange

   decode_operation(owner, (token, family_index, operation_index)):
       require token == owner.hir_snapshot_token else ForeignSnapshot
       family = owner.hir.source_effect_declarations().get(family_index)
           or FamilyOutOfRange
       return family.operations.get(operation_index)
           .map(clone typed SourceOperationId) or OperationOutOfRange

   decode_permission_row(owner, coordinates):
       decode every coordinate in order and collect Result<Vec<_>, Error>
       (never filter, default, truncate, or silently deduplicate)
   ```

   Check the returned `SourceOperationId` values against the R32 covered table
   using structural equality. Check every returned `SourceEffectId` row member
   against the R32 family table and require the decoded row to equal the full
   source row in order and length. Token validation precedes every lookup, and
   all absent/out-of-range family and operation coordinates are errors.

The candidate's existing HIR-relative coordinates are useful only after the
owner adds and serializes the token. Today the archive provides no way to
distinguish coordinates copied from another HIR snapshot. Cross-snapshot
decoding therefore remains OPEN. This is a proposal artifact, not an applied
patch, compile result, or runtime claim.
